// Module 4 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 4

::M4 Q1:: What does the overfit-one-batch test check? {
~Final test accuracy
=That the model and training loop can learn at all#A correct model and loop can drive the loss on one small batch to nearly zero. If not, something basic is broken.
~GPU speed
~Dataset size
}

::M4 Q2:: Which is an example of data leakage? {
~Using augmentation on training images
~Saving checkpoints
=Normalizing with statistics computed on train and test combined before splitting#Information from the test data leaked into preprocessing. Compute statistics on the training data only.
~Using a smaller batch
}

::M4 Q3:: Why call model.eval() before validation? {
=Dropout and batch norm behave differently in training mode#In training mode dropout drops units and batch norm uses batch statistics, so evaluation would be random and wrong.
~It speeds up the GPU
~It resets weights
~It shuffles the data
}

::M4 Q4:: A classifier outputs the same class for every input. Which is the best first check? {
~Buy a bigger GPU
~Add more layers
~Delete the validation set
=Inspect labels, data, and the learning rate#Start with the cheap checks: the data and labels, then the learning rate, before changing the model.
}

::M4 Q5:: Why compare against a simple baseline? {
~To make training faster
=To know whether your model adds real value#If a trivial baseline is as good as your model, the model is adding nothing, or something is wrong.
~To avoid logging
~To reduce parameters
}
